  "body": "## What changed\n\n- New `docs/decisions/1448-start-exit-shared.md`. It records each answer of #3324: the choice, the reason and the dropped options. The issue names this path, so the file uses it in place of `3324-<slug>.md`.\n- New shared type `camcraft_motion::path_picks`: `PathPicks { start, exit }` of `PathPick { xy, z }`, and `PickRole`. The type holds lists. `PathPicks::refusal` refuses a second pick of one role by name. It also refuses a coordinate that is not finite or is more than 1 km from the origin.\n- New `crates/app/src/operation/pick_kinds.rs`:\n  - `PickCapability` (`Ring`, `Region`, `HoleOrder`, `Ends`, `Raster`, `Threading`, `NotTaken(reason)`).\n  - `KindInfo::pick()`, an exhaustive match on `OpType`. 2D Contour is `Ring`. Wire Contour is `Threading`. Probe is `NotTaken` (\"cuts no path\"). Every other kind is `NotTaken(PICK_OWED)` until its family slice of #1448 ships.\n  - `OpParams::path_picks()`, one accessor for every kind. It reads `links.approach.start_point` / `exit_point` and `WireContourOp.start`.\n  - `OpParams::pick_refusal()`. `named_refusal` now calls it in place of the old hard-coded match.\n- MCP: the `params` description of `edit_operation` names `links.approach.start_point` and `links.approach.exit_point` and the kinds that take them. Each kind of `list_operation_types` has a `start_exit` answer (`start`, `exit`, and `field` or `why_not`).\n- UI: every operation page draws the Start point and Exit point groups. A kind that does not take a pick shows one line in each group: \"Not taken - <reason>\". The line is on the Lead in / Lead out tab, or on Geometry when the kind has no lead tab. The contour keeps its editable rows.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe maintainer could not see a start or exit point on the 2D Offset (#1448, 2026-11-22). Only the closed 2D Contour took a pick. The refusal on other kinds did not name the kind. No page said that the pick is not taken. The family slices of #1448 had no shared mechanism.\n\n## Message change\n\nThe refusal of a pick on a kind that does not take it was:\n`a start point is taken only by the 2D contour so far - clear it on this operation`.\nIt is now, for example:\n`2D Offset: a start point is not taken - the planner chooses the entry and the exit of this kind until its slice of #1448 ships; clear it on this operation`.\nThe tilted contour refusal does not change.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins:\n- `crates/app/tests/start_exit_shared.rs` (new, 4 tests):\n  - `a_pick_on_a_kind_that_does_not_take_it_names_the_kind_and_the_reason`\n  - `every_kind_has_one_pick_capability_and_only_the_taken_ones_take_a_pick`\n  - `path_picks_reads_the_contour_pick_and_the_wire_start`\n  - `the_mcp_doors_name_the_pick_fields_and_the_kinds_that_take_them`\n- `egui_app::start_exit_rows::tests::kinds_without_a_picked_start_say_so_by_name`. It was `kinds_without_a_picked_start_draw_neither_group`. The expected behaviour changed on purpose. It now also covers the 2D Offset.\n\nRed before the fix: the two MCP tests ran on unchanged code and failed. The refusal said \"taken only by the 2D contour so far\" with no kind name. The schema said only \"Fields to change\". The other two tests use the new API.\n\nMutations:\n- `sane.rs` from `upstream/main`: `a_pick_on_a_kind_that_does_not_take_it_names_the_kind_and_the_reason` is red. Restored: green.\n- The `not_taken_groups` call in `op_page.rs` removed: `kinds_without_a_picked_start_say_so_by_name` is red. Restored: green.\n\nUnchanged and green: `contour_start_point` (8 tests, with the golden `contour_start_point.cl`), and the start / exit UI tests (`start_exit_rows`, `start_exit_pick`, `start_exit_viewport`).\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` ran 347 steps, and 346 passed. The one red step was `machine::a_kind_that_is_not_a_kind_refuses_at_the_door`. Upstream fixed that test in 80e8891e0 after the branch point (the router kind of #3279). After a merge of `upstream/main`, these pass: `machine` (33), `start_exit_shared` (4), `contour_start_point` (8) and the UI `start_exit` tests (13).\nClippy: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The storage move to one operation-level `picks` key, and the load tests of the old `links.approach.start_point` key and the old wire `start` key. They are in #3339. The decision file says why: the move changes every path variant, and more than ten open PRs change `wire_edm.rs` / `wire_edm_dto.rs`.\n- The shared ring helpers (`nearest_on_ring`, `reach`, `lead_held`) do not move yet. They move with the first family slice that calls them.\n- The viewport snap for `Region`, `HoleOrder`, `Ends` and `Raster`. No kind has these capabilities yet.\n- No planner changes. The family sub-issues of #1448 do that.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nThese open PRs touch nearby code. No open PR changes the same function. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #3283, #3251, #3103, #3058, #2890 and #2831 change `kinds.rs`. This PR does not change `kinds.rs`. A PR that adds an `OpType` must add an arm to `KindInfo::pick()` in `pick_kinds.rs`. The match is exhaustive on purpose.\n- #3251 changes `mcp/edit.rs`. This PR does not change it.\n- #3304 changes `approach_page.rs`. This PR does not change it.\n\nChangelog: Every operation page shows the Start point and Exit point groups; a kind that does not take a pick yet says so by name, the refusal of such a pick names the kind, and MCP `edit_operation` / `list_operation_types` say which kinds take a pick.\n\nEffort: max\n\nFixes #3324\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
